set_option autoImplicit false
-- FG circuit pilot S2s: port of Tools.ShippingChildDepthC onto the context-predicate bundles (RefLawsAOpsX / RefLawsATeleX); generated by a rename-only script (names + suffix X, `AdmCtx O.quiet` -> `O.adm`). No sorry/axiom/native_decide/TRUSTED/law.

/-! # The cache-coherent depth induction (`JQCX`)

PROVED here:
* `ChildKeepsCX O D` / `BodyKeepsCX O D` / `BodyStepCX O` (the `JQCX` analogues of DepthA's);
* `childKeepsC_of_bodyX`, **`childKeepsC_allX`** (induction on `limit - D`), from `core_tripleACX`
  (CoreC) and `synthesizeChild_tripleC'X` (CoreC); `childEntryA_of_childKeepsCX`;
* the OUTERMOST entry from `JQ` (no cache half): `core0_tripleACX` / `full0_tripleACX`
  — exceptions before the clear are `EQ` (= `JQ ∧ OkExc`: `ioEnv`/`profLog`/`depthGet`/the sets
  run with NO `CacheInvAX`), the clear (`tripleC_clearX`) establishes `CacheInvAX`, from there the
  invariant is `JQCX`, and the exception class is weakened `EQCX → EQ` at the end;
  `core_tripleAC_of_bodiesX` / `full_tripleAC_of_bodiesX` discharge CoreC's `hbodyC` from `BodyStepCX`;
* the endpoint `closeInstsM_realCX`: a `RealChildAX` for every child the run returned, cache hits
  included, from `BodyStepCX` alone;
* `bodyStepC_certifiedX` (certified-shape constants, generic-I `fromConst_certified_keepsAPX` +
  `translate_keepsAX` at `I := JQCX O D`) and [removed at integration: `bodyStepC_of_generic`, superseded by ComposeC `bodyStepC_of_tele`] (the body from unit D's generic-I
  front-end lemma, taken as a HYPOTHESIS `hgen`).

NOT proved here (PREMISE/OPEN): `BodyStepCX O` itself — the mixed / machine branches await unit D's
restricted FrontA (generic in `I`), the legacy tail (`hlegacy`) and the five handler premises
`LegacyImplAX LegacyCachedAX CanonKeyAX ProjFieldNameAX` (at `JQCX O D`). `RealChildAX` is a HISTORY of
past synthesis results, not semantic correctness in the current environment. -/

